  "scope_limits": [
    "Review and finite tests do not establish absence of every bug.",
    "Actual storage qualification covers one pinned q35/TCG single-CPU modernVirtIO block profile with QEMU11.1.0 and acquiredOVMF10.2.0. Earlier SMP profiles run their previous subsystems; concurrent storage onSMP,physical hardware,IOMMU and real power-loss behavior are not qualified.",
    "DDF remains a bounded kernel-resident polling transport with four slots,16 descriptors,4KiB bounce operations and512-byte logical sectors. Interrupt dispatch,hotplug/reinsert,surprise-removal recovery,suspend/resume,MSI/MSI-X,multiple controllers and arbitrary scatter/gather are not implemented capabilities.",
    "Actual guest reset is exercised with a published scratch write; device hang,reset-never-acknowledged and malformed hardware completions are covered by ownership code review/host models rather than independently malicious-device QEMU injection.",
    "Cache/mount access requires exclusive serialized ownership and no external media mutation. Short-I/O is injected through real successful-prefix device operations; it does not emulate every physical controller partial-failure mode.",
    "Ext2 is a nonproduction one-group direct-block development subset with flat ASCII names,48KiB maximum files and one4KiB coherent page. Dirty media is rejected; there is no journal,replay,repair or crash-atomic transaction guarantee. P07 owns recovery/security metadata and Windows namespace work.",
    "FAT32 is read-only and bounded to a flat short-name root; initfs is immutable. Full Unicode semantics,permissions,Windows sharing/deletion,file mappings,notifications and asynchronous VFS operations remain later requirements.",
    "Observed stack margins sample actual storage I/O call sites; they are not a proof of a worst-case stack bound on arbitrary future compiler/code changes.",
    "Retained source/report hashes establish identity within the trusted local workspace; they are not external attestation. The final cumulativeP00-P10 checkpoint and P11-P15 integration remain required future work."
  ],
